

OS (Operating System) is system software that acts as an intermediary between the user, applications, and the computer hardware.


Example
=======
When you open a browser like Chrome:

You click the Chrome icon.
The Operating System loads Chrome into memory.
It allocates CPU time and RAM.
It lets Chrome access files, the internet, keyboard, mouse, and display.
When you close Chrome, the OS frees those resources.

Without an OS, your computer cannot run applications.




Types of Operating Systems
==========================
| Type         | Example                                                 |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| Desktop OS   | Windows, Linux, macOS                                   |
| Mobile OS    | Android, iOS                                            |
| Server OS    | Ubuntu Server, Red Hat Enterprise Linux, Windows Server |
| Real-Time OS | VxWorks, QNX                                            |
| Embedded OS  | FreeRTOS                                                |
